  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "createDummyConnection",
    "file": "open62541/tests/testing-plugins/testing_networklayers.c",
    "description": "The crash is caused by returning a partially initialized UA_Connection from createDummyConnection: the struct field `free` is never set. The PoV drives error handling in UA_Server_processBinaryMessage (open62541/src/server/ua_server_binary.c), which closes the connection and later cleanup calls UA_Connection_deleteMembers(&c). That cleanup path invokes connection->free, resulting in an indirect call through an uninitialized/wild function pointer and a jump to heap data (matching the wild PC crash).",
    "conditions": "Data flow: fuzz_binary_message.cc creates a dummy connection via createDummyConnection, feeds attacker-controlled binary chunks to UA_Server_processBinaryMessage, then always performs teardown (c.close and UA_Connection_deleteMembers). For this PoV, malformed message sequence triggers failure/close path and then teardown reaches UA_Connection_deleteMembers on the dummy connection. Because createDummyConnection did not initialize `c.free`, teardown performs a wild function-pointer call. Trigger requires using this test dummy connection plus any input that reaches the teardown path (the provided PoV does)."
  },
